// The Gran Canaria route cluster: airport-to-destination, hotels, cruise
// port, resort-to-resort, and day-trip transfers.
//
// Core hub pages are NOT duplicated here:
//   - /gran-canaria/ + /es/gran-canaria/ (NEW CityRecord, mainAirportIata "LPA")
//   - /gran-canaria-airport-transfer/ + /es/traslado-aeropuerto-gran-canaria/ (existing AirportRecord LPA)
//   - /las-palmas-de-gran-canaria/ + /es/las-palmas-de-gran-canaria/ (NEW CityRecord, mainAirportIata "LPA")
//
// One-airport architecture: unlike Bilbao/Tenerife, Gran Canaria has only
// one major airport (LPA), so the "two CityRecords" pattern here isn't
// driven by a second airport — it exists because the spec explicitly wants
// both an island-wide commercial hub AND a distinct capital-city hub, same
// as Bilbao's Bilbao/San Sebastián split. Both CityRecords reference LPA;
// "gran-canaria" is listed first in lib/cities/data.ts so it's the one
// `cities.find(c => c.mainAirportIata === iata)` resolves to for the
// airport page's own Related Transfers widget. Routes are filed under
// whichever hub makes more sense for that specific pair regardless of
// which CityRecord "wins" that lookup — e.g. the airport-to-Las-Palmas
// pair itself uses originCitySlug "las-palmas-de-gran-canaria" so that
// city's own hub gets genuine route coverage too.
//
// Maspalomas, Playa del Inglés, Meloneras, San Agustín, Puerto Rico, Puerto
// de Mogán, Mogán, Arguineguín, Taurito, and Vecindario have NO CityRecord
// of their own (matching the Costa Adeje/Los Cristianos precedent from
// Tenerife and the Getxo/Hondarribia precedent from Bilbao) — they are
// covered as route-cluster destination pages only, avoiding thin
// near-duplicate hub pages competing with their own route pages for the
// same search intent.
//
// Resort-to-resort pairs WITHIN the contiguous eastern strip (Maspalomas /
// Playa del Inglés / San Agustín / Meloneras — all sub-5-minute drives in
// one built-up conurbation) were deliberately NOT built as separate route
// pages — each area gets its own airport-pair page instead, with the short
// hops between them covered as prose context. Resort-to-resort pages were
// only built connecting the genuinely distinct eastern strip (anchored by
// Maspalomas) to the western strip (Puerto Rico / Puerto de Mogán /
// Arguineguín / Taurito).
//
// NO per-hotel pages were skipped this time — unlike Tenerife's spec, this
// one explicitly asked for a curated hotel batch. 6 verified, currently-
// operating, geographically-balanced hotels were selected after a research
// pass corrected a wrong assumption (Radisson Blu Resort Gran Canaria is in
// Arguineguín/Patalavaca, not Meloneras).
//
// NO inter-island routes were built (Gran Canaria<->Tenerife or any other
// island) and NO mainland Spain routes — a private car cannot cross open
// water, so there is no genuine door-to-door service to sell; matches the
// identical, already-documented decision in tenerife.ts.
//
// Uses the generic relationship engine (lib/routes/related.ts,
// lib/routes/coverage.ts) with zero city-specific logic.
//
